expo-widgets 58.0.19 (Android) needs two upstream fixes that expo main has
merged but no expo-widgets release contains yet.

1. Build fix, expo/expo#51654 ("[expo-widgets] Fix the Android build of
   custom notifications"). The custom-notification sources import Peek under
   `io.github.jakex7.peek.*`, while the package's Gradle dependency
   `io.github.expo.peek:peek-emittables:0.3.2` (and the transitive
   peek-notification 0.3.2) ships its classes under `io.github.expo.peek.*`,
   so `:expo-widgets:compileDebugKotlin` fails with "Unresolved reference
   'jakex7'". The patch renames those imports.

2. Launch crash fix, expo/expo#51655 ("[expo-widgets] Fix the Android crash
   at launch from CustomNotification"). `WidgetsModule` registers the
   `CustomNotification` SharedObject with `Class(...)` but no `Constructor`,
   and expo-modules-core 58.0.15+ rejects that while it builds the module, so
   every Android launch fails with "constructor cannot be null" before any JS
   runs. The patch adds a constructor that throws
   `CustomNotificationCreationException`, matching upstream exactly.

Remove this patch when the app moves to an expo-widgets release that
contains both expo/expo#51654 and expo/expo#51655.

